      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "<ico-envelope></ico-envelope> THE 6 PARTS OF AN EMAIL",
      "intro": "Un email profesional tiene siempre estas seis partes, en este orden. Si falta una, se nota.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "cells",
          "cells": [
            {
              "h": "1 · Subject line",
              "body": "Meeting Request: Q2 Sales Strategy"
            },
            {
              "h": "2 · Greeting",
              "body": "Dear Mr. Smith, / Dear Hiring Manager,"
            },
            {
              "h": "3 · Opening",
              "body": "I hope you are doing well. I am writing to…"
            },
            {
              "h": "4 · Body",
              "body": "Your main point, in clear paragraphs."
            },
            {
              "h": "5 · Closing",
              "body": "I look forward to your reply."
            },
            {
              "h": "6 · Sign-off",
              "body": "Best regards, / Sincerely,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "phrases",
          "items": [
            {
              "en": "I hope you are doing well.",
              "sp": "Apertura cordial."
            },
            {
              "en": "I am writing to follow up on the report.",
              "sp": "Dices por qué escribes, en la primera línea."
            },
            {
              "en": "Could you please send me the report?",
              "sp": "Pedido educado."
            },
            {
              "en": "I would appreciate it if you could reply by Friday.",
              "sp": "Todavía más formal."
            },
            {
              "en": "I look forward to your reply.",
              "sp": "Cierre clásico: quedo atento a tu respuesta."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "gold": true,
          "body": "<b>Dos preposiciones que se escapan:</b> <s class='x'>I look forward your reply.</s> → <span class='ok'>I look forward to your reply.</span> · <s class='x'>Would you mind to send it?</s> → <span class='ok'>Would you mind sending it?</span>"
        }
      ],
      "stage": "① EMAIL STRUCTURE <span class=\"es\">· partes + cortesía</span>"
